    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [x] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version of the `main` branch\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.pick\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.12.x\n\n### Description\n\nIn mini.pick preview of a file in neovim 0.12 the floating window shows my statusbar due to the new neovim 12 feature of showing statusbar in floating windows.\nI can hackly disable it, but it seems unintended and it would definitely be better for the plugin to disable this functionality ootb.\n\nBut by seeing the statusbar it allowed me to spot another bug:\nMy statusbar displays filename. And in place of the filename in the floating window statusbar i see: `minipick://(number)/preview`. If i perform any of the following actions (move up, down, toggle preview) the number gets incremented. This doesn't affect functionality, and a buffer overflow is not something likely to happen, but i still think its worth mentioning.\n\n### Reproduction\n\n1. install mini.pick with vim.pack\n2. launch mini.pick, toggle preview of any file",
