            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the issue!\n\nIt is most certainly indeed a result of Neovim>=0.12 now allowing to show statusline in a floating window. By default 'mini.pick' doesn't show any statusline, but it can not prevent user forcing to show it.\n\nThis is a similar situation to #2342 and is probably the result of how the statusline showing is set up. I'd need a more detailed steps to reproduce the issue, because with only two current steps it does not reproduce. Maybe 'mini.pick' can try to not trigger some basic event.\n\n---\n\n> My statusbar displays filename. And in place of the filename in the floating window statusbar i see: `minipick://(number)/preview`. If i perform any of the following actions (move up, down, toggle preview) the number gets incremented. This doesn't affect functionality, and a buffer overflow is not something likely to happen, but i still think its worth mentioning.\n\nYes, this is expected and is how preview in 'mini.pick' works.",
